From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:07:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: fast scroller hit box stays on the drawn thumb
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A fling leaves the thumb visible for the fade delay. The hit rectangle
was 32 dp, grown toward the content, and startDragImmediately consumes
the down. A swipe that started in that strip, including one that began
during the coast, dragged the thumb. The list jumped by the scroll
ratio and the release had no coast.

The hit rectangle is now ThumbThickness plus endInset. A down on the
drawn thumb still drags immediately. A down anywhere else scrolls the
content, including while the thumb is visible after a fling.

VerticalFastScroller, VerticalGridFastScroller, VerticalMasonryFastScroller,
and IrregularVerticalGridFastScroller share HarmonyScrollerThumb.
ThumbTouchWidth is gone.

Tests: PanoramaMasonryFlingTest (Robolectric) and
PanoramaMasonryFlingLogicTest. Robolectric 4.16.1 and ui-test stay.
junit-vintage is 6.0.3, matching this tree's JUnit. The Compose test
entry is androidx.compose.ui.test.runComposeUiTest; this BOM has no
ui.test.v2. preview's matchingFallbacks is release, so
debugImplementation(ui-test-manifest) is not in the preview APK.

与 mihon-harmony 0032 同源。
